= Levi's crisis.

n a result that shocked everyone—including his fellow leftists—former communist Paul Levi secured the leadership with the backing of Kurt Rosenfeld. This upset was made possible as the Left Social Democrats captured key positions in parliamentary factions and councils, while also gaining ground in the control commission and even in executive committee by replacing several veteran members. Levi’s victory sparked immediate outrage among party elites, old-guard leaders, centrist ideologues, Staatspolitiker pragmatists, and trade union officials, many of whom are demanding the congress results be annulled and the left purged from leadership. Alarmed by the reaction, Levi and Rosenfeld are preparing for an all-out struggle to defend their gains. 